# Your Name — Skills & Experience Reference

Use this file when generating tailored applications. Pull from this, don't invent.

Copy this file to `PROFILE_REFERENCE.md` (gitignored — it's personal and
shouldn't be committed) and fill in your own background. This is the
source of truth the `apply-to-posting` skill draws from when drafting
cover letters and resumes for postings tracked in Swamp.

---

## Career Arc

A short paragraph framing your overall trajectory: what kind of roles you've
held, what you're known for, what you're looking for next, and any
constraints worth stating up front (location, remote/onsite, seniority
level). Note anything you want every draft to consistently avoid or lead
with (e.g. "don't lead with years of experience").

---

## Experience

### Company Name — Title (Start–End)

A one-line note on how central this role is and what to pull from it.

- Bullet point describing a concrete accomplishment, with **key
  technologies/skills** bolded so they're easy to scan
- Another accomplishment — quantify impact where you can (scale, latency,
  team size, revenue, etc.)
- ...

**Framing options:**

- Which angle to lead with when this role is most relevant (e.g. "backend
  engineering angle: ...")
- Another possible angle

